      "writtenOn": "2021-02-26T23:37:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a way to reuse some of the same codepaths for the disconnecting and disconnected states; we could have subclasses that differ in just the \"next\" state behavior, but that also adds more layers of indirection.\n\nWe\u0027d need at least 2 (additional) shell states:\n  - DisconnectingExiting extends DisconnectingState\n  - DisconnectingRetry extends DisconnectingState\n\nAdditionally, that makes switching from a DisconnectingRetry to DisconnectingExiting more complex, in that we\u0027d have to audit the enter() and exit() methods of the states to avoid double-closing, or resetting teardown timeout alarms. (or we can mix the inheritence and parent-child-state patterns, which would make for a readability nightmare)",
      "parentUuid": "8f2ed429_47b7e572",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1141,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1141,
        "endChar": 22
